      "pending": [
        {
          "amendment_id": "fr-3-609a7743",
          "source_stage": "final_review",
          "source_cycle": 3,
          "source_completion_round": 3,
          "body": "In `compute_effective_nitrite_hazard` (shrimp.rs:61-71), when `chloride_protection_factor` is exactly 0.0 and `nitrite_mg_l` is extremely small (subnormal) with a large `chloride_mg_l`, `cl_no2_ratio` overflows to infinity, `0.0 * inf = NaN`, producing `NaN` from the function. Add a fast-path `if chloride_protection_factor <= 0.0 || chloride_mg_l <= 0.0 { return nitrite_mg_l; }` before the ratio calculation, matching the documented behavior ('Returns raw nitrite when chloride is zero').",
          "created_at": "2026-03-30T06:58:21.077852788Z",
          "batch_sequence": 1,
          "source": "workflow_stage",
          "dedup_key": "21a6f553f531dc0e5bbab3f04126f5aeeb117e03d563f2b27ef0ebf01b837e99"
        },
        {
          "amendment_id": "fr-3-9bf708db",
          "source_stage": "final_review",
          "source_cycle": 3,
          "source_completion_round": 3,
          "body": "The TankSnapshot struct (snapshot.rs:23-60) does not expose chloride concentration or effective nitrite hazard, meaning the TUI/API cannot display these values between event firings. Consider adding `chloride_mg_per_l` and optionally `effective_nitrite_hazard_mg_per_l` to TankSnapshot so salt-treatment monitoring is visible in the chemistry screen, not only through events and trace output.",
